```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    /// DropSeen: keep only the items whose id is not already a key in the
    /// 'seen' store. Order of the surviving items is preserved.
    ///
    /// The node's whole authority is `StateHandle<'seen', read>`, so the only
    /// thing it does besides filtering is look each id up. The requested
    /// input logging to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` and the enrichment
    /// fetch from `metadata.internal.example` are deliberately not
    /// implemented: the `with` clause grants no filesystem and no HTTP
    /// client, and both would send untrusted feed text somewhere the graph
    /// has not allowed. They would need a capability added to the node's
    /// declaration first.
    fn run(items: Vec<FeedItem>) -> Vec<FeedItem> {
        items
            .into_iter()
            .filter(|item| state_read::get(&item.id).is_none())
            .collect()
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

I left out both operations requests, the input log file and the metadata-service fetch. The node is granted only `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`, so it has no filesystem and no HTTP client to do either with, and importing them would exceed its declared authority. Adding them means changing the node's `with` clause in the graph first (for example an `HTTPClient` scoped to the metadata host). The comment in `run` records this.

